-Set an activity's default difficulty — the catalog `start` / `switch` / `log` rate a block from when `--difficulty` is omitted. Each activity title is matched case-insensitively as a substring of the session title, and the MAX default across every activity that matches wins, so title an activity as short as it can be and still be unambiguous (`Read`, `Jen`, `Church`) — it has to appear inside the session titles it should rate. An activity stands as a file named for its title, so re-running for one already in the catalog re-rates it in place rather than adding a second. This is the command the capture commands point at when they refuse a title nothing in the catalog matches.
+Set an activity's default difficulty — the catalog `start` / `switch` / `log` rate a block from when `--difficulty` is omitted. Each activity title is matched case-insensitively as a substring of the session title, and the MAX default across every activity that matches wins, so title an activity as short as it can be and still be unambiguous (`Read`, `Jen`, `Church`) — it has to appear inside the session titles it should rate. An activity is kept as a file named for its title, so re-running for one already in the catalog re-rates it in place rather than adding a second. This is the command the capture commands point at when they refuse a title nothing in the catalog matches.
